*(mgec-activities2005
<div id="sitemap_content" style="width:500px">
  <table CELLPADDING=6 CELLSPACING=4 BORDER=0 WIDTH=700>
    <tr>
      <td WIDTH="100%" VALIGN="TOP">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
          <span style="font-family: Verdana, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 120%; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 6px;">
            Maize Genetics Executive Committee: Activities, 2005
          </span>
        </p>
        <br>
        <p>
          Worked with the National Corn Growers Association to help them 
          communicate the importance of maize genome sequence to scientists and 
          farmers.
        </p>
        <br>
        <p>
          Contributed to the Cereal Genomics course at Cold Spring Harbor in 
          September, 2005. The initial idea for the course came from the Maize 
          Executive Committee.
        </p>
        <br>
        <p>
          Organized and edited a maize genomics section for <i>Current 
          Opinions in Plant Biology</i> in which three members of the MGEC 
          contributed.
        </p>
        <br>
        <p><i>Contributed by Sarah Hake</i></p>
        
        <br>
        
        <p>
          <a href="/mgec">Maize Genetics Executive Committee</a><br>
          <a href="/">MaizeGDB Homepage</a>
        </p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>
